* Simplified behavioural model of ONE LM358 amplifier, written for circuit-tutor.
* NOT the vendor macro-model: single dominant pole, no slew limit. Aol = 1e5 (100 dB),
* GBW = 1 MHz; output swings from VEE + 0.02 V up to VCC - 1.5 V (single-supply behaviour).
* The output current is drawn from VCC when sourcing and returned to VEE when sinking. Swing
* limits are diode clamps on the gain node, driven from ground-referenced copies of the rails.
* Pin order matches the registry unit_line: inp inm vcc vee out
.subckt LM358 inp inm vcc vee out
rin inp inm 1e12
* gain stage: 10 uA/V into 10 Gohm = 1e5, dominant pole at 10 Hz
g1 0 n1 inp inm 10u
r1 n1 0 10g
c1 n1 0 1.592p
* clamps: n1 stays within about (VEE + 0.02 V, VCC - 1.5 V); each offset adds the ~0.05 V drop of a sharp (n = 0.1) diode
erhi rhi 0 vcc 0 1
vhi rhi nhi 1.55
dhi n1 nhi dclamp
erlo rlo 0 vee 0 1
vlo nlo rlo 0.07
dlo nlo n1 dclamp
* output stage
eout n2 0 n1 0 1
rout n2 n3 50
vsense n3 out 0
* move the output current onto the supply pins (smooth split, 1 uA rounding at zero load)
bsrc vcc 0 i = 0.5 * (i(vsense) + sqrt(i(vsense) * i(vsense) + 1e-12))
bsnk 0 vee i = 0.5 * (sqrt(i(vsense) * i(vsense) + 1e-12) - i(vsense))
* quiescent current, about 0.7 mA at 5 V
rq vcc vee 7.1k
.model dclamp d(is=1e-14 n=0.1)
.ends LM358
